            "text": "{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2024}}\n{{Distinguish|Dichondra repens}}"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Dichondra micrantha, the Asian ponysfoot or lawnleaf, is a species of flowering plant in the family Convolvulaceae. It is native to Texas, Mexico, and the Caribbean, and it has been introduced worldwide. A prostrate perennial reaching {{cvt|4|in|cm|0|order=flip}}, it prefers wetter soils. In the past it was recommended as a grass substitute in lawns due to its easy maintenance requirements, but proved vulnerable to flea beetles."
          }
        ]
